#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/shared-code.rst:15
msgid "Shared Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/shared-code.rst:17
msgid ""
"By default, PlatformIO does not build the main source code from the :ref:"
"`projectconf_pio_src_dir` folder in pair with a test source code. If you "
"have a shared/common code between your \"main\" and \"test\" programs, you "
"have 2 options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/shared-code.rst:21
msgid ""
"We recommend splitting the source code into multiple components and placing "
"them into the :ref:`projectconf_pio_lib_dir` (project's private libraries "
"and components). :ref:`ldf` will find and include these libraries "
"automatically in the build process. You can include any library/component "
"header file in your test or main application source code using ``#include "
"<MyComponent.h>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/shared-code.rst:27
msgid ""
"See `Local & Embedded: Calculator <https://github.com/platformio/platformio-"
"examples/tree/develop/unit-testing/calculator>`__ for an example, where we "
"have a \"calculator\" component in the :ref:`projectconf_pio_lib_dir` folder "
"and include it in the tests and the main application using ``#include "
"<calculator.h>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/shared-code.rst:32
msgid ""
"**NOT RECOMMENDED**. Manually instruct PlatformIO to build the main source "
"code from the :ref:`projectconf_pio_src_dir` folder in pair with a test "
"source code using the :ref:`projectconf_test_build_src` option in :ref:"
"`projectconf`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/shared-code.rst:42
msgid ""
"This is very useful if you unit test independent libraries where you can't "
"split source code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/shared-code.rst:46
msgid ""
"Please note that you will need to use ``#ifndef PIO_UNIT_TESTING`` and "
"``#endif`` guard to hide non-test related source code. For example, own "
"``main()``, ``setup() / loop()``, or ``app_main()`` functions."
msgstr ""
